From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: bq256xx: honour the battery charge limits

bq256xx_hw_init() programs the charge current and the charge voltage from
the driver's own defaults, and only uses what monitored-battery says as the
upper bound of the clamp inside the setters:

	bq256xx_set_ichg(bq, bq->chip_info->bq256xx_def_ichg);
	bq256xx_set_vbatreg(bq, bq->chip_info->bq256xx_def_vbatreg);

So a battery description is only able to lower these two, never to raise
them. On the Motorola Moto G82 5G the cell takes 4350 mV, but the bq25601
default is 4208 mV, so the part comes up regulating 4208 mV: it reports the
battery as Full at about 82% and trickles, and roughly a tenth of the
capacity is unreachable until userspace writes constant_charge_voltage by
hand.

The neighbouring calls in the same function already trust the battery
description directly:

	bq256xx_set_iprechg(bq, bat_info->precharge_current_ua);
	bq256xx_set_iterm(bq, bat_info->charge_term_current_ua);

Use it for these two as well. The clamps in the setters still apply, and
when no battery is described the fallback path has already filled bat_info
with those same defaults, so behaviour there is unchanged.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq256xx_charger.c
@@ -1644,7 +1644,7 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	ret = bq->chip_info->bq256xx_set_ichg(bq,
-				bq->chip_info->bq256xx_def_ichg);
+				bat_info->constant_charge_current_max_ua);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -1654,7 +1654,7 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	ret = bq->chip_info->bq256xx_set_vbatreg(bq,
-				bq->chip_info->bq256xx_def_vbatreg);
+				bat_info->constant_charge_voltage_max_uv);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
